      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1857345170,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Thus, setting the GID start point to 102 should fix the issue.\n\nThe line in the script:\n\n`free_gid=$(dscl . -list /Groups PrimaryGroupID | sort -bnk2 | awk -v min_gid=$min_gid 'BEGIN{i=min_gid}{if($2==i)i++}END{print i}')`\n\nis supposed to find the first unused GID from the starting point. Presumably the correct fix is to find out why that's not working.\n\nUnless you have any documentation suggesting that 100 and 101, but not 102, are special GIDs that don't show up with that command.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-04-11T12:22:10.609Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-04-11T18:33:47.882Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 294751863,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
