        },
        {
          "id": 1858235166,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The GID 100 belongs to Print Operator group: \\_lpoperator.  GID 101 is mystery, it doesn't show up by `dscl` query, but it returns group UUID by `dsmemberutil` query. And no group match with this UUID at all from `dscl . -list /Groups GeneratedUID` , as  well as other categories(Users, NetGroups, Config, etc.) in Directory Service.\n\n```\n% dsmemberutil getuuid -g 101 \n3AE28636-B95A-40B7-B0BA-461551CFD8AD\n```\n\nSince these lower than 500 groups are shared and managed by macOS, I don't think Apple provides any document to give insights about group ID assignment convention as always. I am just able to find someone on server fault has a best guess, but I think you all have seen this before. https://serverfault.com/questions/390640/how-are-group-ids-assigned",
          "author": {
            "id": 20835423,
            "username": "shaozx",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "shaozx",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/921a557156120f15a2e1e5bc1d40c16c73ac9553bae2c5754f328a3ac995547a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/shaozx"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-04-11T20:11:49.134Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-04-11T20:11:49.134Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 294751863,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
