        {
          "id": 1858302684,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It is not due to access_bpf this particular group. The gid 101 is in use and conflicted on macOS Sonoma, and it not queryable who actually used for this gid 101. Here is an example I created a gid 101 for group name test_gp1. \n\n```\n% sudo dseditgroup -v -o create -i 101 -r \"Test existence\" test_gp1\ndseditgroup verbose mode\nOptions selected by user:\nCreate option selected\nUsername determined to be <root>\nGID provided as <101>\nRealname provided as <Test existence>\nGroupname provided as <test_gp1>\n\nSkipping authentication because user has effective ID 0\nGID already exists\n\n% echo $?\n64\n\n% sudo dseditgroup -o read test_gp1\ndsAttrTypeStandard:GeneratedUID -\n\t\t67DAEBFF-8F9E-49C9-A116-5FE536E6AA8B\ndsAttrTypeStandard:RecordName -\n\t\ttest_gp1\ndsAttrTypeStandard:RecordType -\n\t\tdsRecTypeStandard:Groups\ndsAttrTypeStandard:AppleMetaNodeLocation -\n\t\t/Local/Default\n\n% sudo dscl . -list /Groups PrimaryGroupID | grep -c 101\n0\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 20835423,
            "username": "shaozx",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "shaozx",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/921a557156120f15a2e1e5bc1d40c16c73ac9553bae2c5754f328a3ac995547a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/shaozx"
          },
